  "decision": "NO_CHANGE",
  "workflow_yaml": null,
  "rationale": "No supported workflow_yaml optimization applies. The workflow already caches the Maven repository (~/.m2/repository) with a monthly key, so P-LIT-GHA-CACHE is contraindicated because an equivalent cache already exists. P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT cannot be safely applied because there is no representative successful-duration history (ci_history shows five consecutive scheduled failures and no successful runs), so a timeout budget cannot be derived without risking interruption of valid slow deploy runs. P-LIT-FAIL-SCHEDULE matches the repeated-failure signal but is ci_service scope, requires an approved monitored pause/resume policy and owner notification/recovery path, and is contraindicated for a periodic snapshot deploy that serves as a required scheduled check; it cannot be implemented as a minimal workflow YAML change. Other patterns (matrix fail-fast, change filtering, stale-run cancellation, test prioritization/selection, Bazel tuning) do not fit this single-job scheduled Maven deploy workflow or would alter required coverage.",
  "evidence_ids": ["P-LIT-GHA-CACHE", "P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT", "P-LIT-FAIL-SCHEDULE"]
}
